{"title":"Distinct","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Definition\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Definition</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Examples\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Examples</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2\"><a href=\"#Introductory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2\"><a href=\"#Intermediate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2\"><a href=\"#Olympiad\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Olympiad</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition\">Definition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distinct&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Distinct</b> is a commonly used word in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competitions\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competitions\">mathematics competitions</a> meaning different.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Examples\">Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distinct&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>Distinct <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number\" title=\"Number\">numbers</a> are numbers which are not <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equal\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Equal\">equal</a> to each other.</li>\n<li>Distinct <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">sets</a> are sets which are not equal to each other.</li>\n<li>Distinct <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polygons\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Polygons\">polygons</a> are polygons which are not <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Congruent_(geometry)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Congruent (geometry)\">congruent</a> to each other.</li>\n<li>Distinct objects are objects which are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distinguishability\" title=\"Distinguishability\">distinguishable</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Exampleprob&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory\">Introductory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Exampleprob&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-2\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>Let the letters <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> represent distinct digits. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/a/8ca56c9bfd7c62759b8c5e4d08af1c54279e3c53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{F}~\\underline{L}~\\underline{Y}~\\underline{F}~\\underline{L}~\\underline{Y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" /> is the greatest number that satisfies the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/047513b257239e4538e713105a012a223b79ded7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8\\cdot\\underline{F}~\\underline{L}~\\underline{Y}~\\underline{F}~\\underline{L}~\\underline{Y}=\\underline{B}~\\underline{U}~\\underline{G}~\\underline{B}~\\underline{U}~\\underline{G}.\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"15\" /> What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/5/a95dfcbcaec76652ae649387381bf08beb82403f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{F}~\\underline{L}~\\underline{Y}+\\underline{B}~\\underline{U}~\\underline{G}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />?<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/4/6640f8c5138b8919fc7c546cefeba8f1a737cca6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1089 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 1098 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 1107 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 1116 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 1125\\]\" width=\"483\" height=\"17\" /></li></ul>\n<p>(<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2024 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">Source</a>)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Exampleprob&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-3\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>Call a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> extra-distinct if the remainders when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e52f1f7ea7d73821261dc410f229346e3ddd6b09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3, 4, 5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are distinct. Find the number of extra-distinct positive integers less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>(<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">Source</a>)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Olympiad\">Olympiad</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Exampleprob&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-4\" title=\"Edit section: Olympiad\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>Given any set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/f/59f586d0452f0ce847ac06fa9b8a0024ccfffd41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\{a_1, a_2, a_3, a_4\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" /> of four distinct positive integers, we denote the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/3/75391109812e189de2b8ed57268ad22206a03c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 +a_2 +a_3 +a_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4ea2f9ce788b497a2d5d56c3205ad0c82f9df92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/d/2fdb780be66bfbfb3082563bb7e174790920da0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"10\" /> denote the number of pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/1/811480f547c16afc74ffca555e4fd6c166ccfa68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/6/dd6b1448ab9467cabf3bfde844192a67dd2fd434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq  i &lt; j \\leq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f57d5835a2f3454339c4378672a1fd0bc7d3abd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i +a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4ea2f9ce788b497a2d5d56c3205ad0c82f9df92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. Find all sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> of four distinct positive integers which achieve the largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/d/2fdb780be66bfbfb3082563bb7e174790920da0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"10\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>(<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Source</a>)\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Distinct&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018082846\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.079 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 111/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1884/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 1412/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4769/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   55.410      1 -total\n 89.92%   49.824      1 Template:Exampleprob\n  9.53%    5.281      1 Template:Stub\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22071:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018082846 and revision id 235471. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}